<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Colony mechs are gated by a whitelist, not a blacklist. Verse.Pawn.GetDisabledWorkTypes walks
    every WorkTypeDef in the database and, under if (ModsConfig.BiotechActive && IsColonyMech), adds
    to the DISABLED list every one that is not in RaceProps.mechEnabledWorkTypes. Mech_Constructoid
    ships that list with Construction alone, so WorkType_Improving is disabled for it until it is
    added here. Nothing in C# can fix this: the whitelist is read live off the race def.

    Constructoid only, of the seven mechs that declare the field. It is the one that already carries
    Construction. Lifter has Hauling, Tunneler Mining, Fabricor the five production types, Agrihand
    PlantCutting and Growing, Cleansweeper Cleaning, Paramedic Doctor and Firefighter. A player who
    wants another one can copy the operation and change the defName.

    A mech is judged on RaceProperties.mechFixedSkillLevel, which defaults to 10 and which no shipped
    def overrides, so a constructoid improves as a Construction 10 worker. Under the Default preset
    that reaches Good but not Excellent.

    On <success>: the xpath cannot match without Biotech, because the Mech_Constructoid def is then
    not in the document at all, and a missed xpath otherwise logs a red error naming this file at the
    end of def loading. Always makes it a silent no-op instead.

    Do NOT reach for MayRequire here. ModContentPack.LoadPatches deserialises every <Operation> child
    unconditionally and reads no MayRequire attribute; the MayRequire check in LoadedModManager
    applies to def nodes after patching, not to operations. It would look like a gate and be nothing.
    Note also that <success> is a child ELEMENT: DirectXmlToObject maps only child nodes onto fields,
    so success="Always" written as an attribute is silently ignored.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <success>Always</success>
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="Mech_Constructoid"]/race/mechEnabledWorkTypes</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>WorkType_Improving</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
